.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH morshd 8  "morshd 0.3.0"
.SH NAME
morshd \- morshd \- Next\-generation resilient QUIC SSH daemon (combining Mosh & SSH3)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmorshd\fR [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-listen\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-listen\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-completions\fR] [\fB\-\-man\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-cert\fR] [\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-stealth\-knock\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\-keys\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-password\fR] [\fB\-\-pam\-service\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-auth\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
morshd \- Next\-generation resilient QUIC SSH daemon (combining Mosh & SSH3)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-listen\fR \fI<LISTEN>\fR
Socket address to listen on for incoming UDP/QUIC traffic (default: 0.0.0.0:2222)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-listen\fR \fI<TCP_LISTEN>\fR
Optional explicit socket address to listen on for TCP fallback (defaults to same port as \-\-listen)
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Optional path to server TOML configuration file (defaults to /etc/morsh/morshd.toml)
.TP
\fB\-\-completions\fR \fI<SHELL>\fR
Generate shell completions for the specified shell (bash, zsh, fish) and exit
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
bash
.IP \(bu 2
elvish
.IP \(bu 2
fish
.IP \(bu 2
powershell
.IP \(bu 2
zsh
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-man\fR
Generate man page (roff format) to stdout and exit
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-cert\fR \fI<CERT>\fR
Optional path to TLS certificate chain in PEM format
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-key\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
Optional path to TLS private key in PEM format (PKCS#8)
.TP
\fB\-\-stealth\-knock\fR \fI<STEALTH_KNOCK>\fR
Optional stealth knock path prefix (SSH3 style anti\-scanning defense)
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\-keys\fR \fI<AUTH_KEYS>\fR
Optional explicit path to authorized_keys file (defaults to ~/.ssh/authorized_keys per user)
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-password\fR
Allow Linux PAM / password authentication
.TP
\fB\-\-pam\-service\fR \fI<PAM_SERVICE>\fR
PAM service name to use for password authentication (default: morsh)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-auth\fR
Permit unauthenticated connections (testing / development only)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose debug logging
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
